==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[apples to oranges]]

===Noun===
{{head|en|noun|head=[[apples]] [[and]] [[oranges]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} Said of a comparison of items that are not comparable.
#: ''It's '''apples and oranges'''.  You can't convert square meters to linear inches.''
#: ''Comparing the grades of English students to Engineering students is like trying to compare '''apples and oranges.'''''

====Antonyms====
* [[apples to apples]], [[apples with apples]]
* [[apples to apples, oranges to oranges]]
* [[oranges with oranges]] {{qualifier|rare}}

====Related terms====
* [[mix apples and oranges]]

